two years ago today three white men  chased down and murdered ahmad aarberry  that is not in dispute and now neither  is their motivation the family of arbury  is still mourning the loss but now  they're also celebrating a victory in  federal court travis mcmichael his  father gregory and their neighbor  william roddy bryan were convicted of  hate crimes these cases are very rare  and notoriously difficult for the  justice department to pursue  but the prosecution succeeded in finding  evidence that the defendants had a  history of racism and acted on it janet  chamblin spoke to arbory's mother after  yesterday's verdict  when are the hardest moments for you  wanda waking up every morning  knowing that ahmad is gone  and he's not going to be here today like  he wasn't here yesterday  wanda cooper jones knows tuesday's  verdict will never bring her son back  but that doesn't mean it wasn't welcome  news why was this federal trial  important to you  the world knew that ahmad was murdered  however the world needed to know  the mindsets of the men that who  actually murdered the mod and that these  guys were racist  was murdered simply because he was a he  was a black man  it was the second time in three months  the ivory family and legal team won  their fight as gregory and travis  mcmichael and william roddy bryan were  found guilty  all three now face life in prison for  federal hate crimes in addition to their  life sentences for their murder  convictions attorney general merrick  garland praised the ruling i cannot  imagine the pain that a mother  feels  to have her son  run down and then gunned down  while taking a jog on a public street  wanda cooper jones plans to keep that  fight going in honor of her son  this is a burden you've been carrying  for two years now are you able to  continue to fight for the change that  you want to see happen or are you spent  i must continue to fight like i should  earlier i don't think a mother should go  through the heartbreak 